# User Types and Roles Guide

## User Roles
The application supports two distinct user roles defined in [user.ts](mdc:src/types/user.ts):

1. STUDENT
   - For medical students seeking opportunities
   - Includes education details
   - Can save and apply to opportunities
   - Has skills and interests fields

2. FACILITY
   - For medical facilities offering opportunities
   - Includes location and contact information
   - Can post and manage opportunities
   - Has specialties and facility type fields

## User Schema
The Mongoose schema in [User.ts](mdc:src/models/User.ts) implements:

### Base Fields
- name (required)
- email (required, unique)
- password (required, hashed)
- role (required, enum of UserRole)
- timestamps (createdAt, updatedAt)

### Student-specific Fields
```typescript
education: {
  school: string
  major: string
  graduationYear: number
  gpa: number
}
skills: string[]
interests: string[]
```

### Facility-specific Fields
```typescript
facilityInfo: {
  type: 'hospital' | 'clinic' | 'private practice' | 'other'
  specialties: string[]
  location: {
    address: string
    city: string
    state: string
    zipCode: string
    coordinates: {
      lat: number
      lng: number
    }
  }
  contact: {
    phone: string
    website: string
  }
}
```

## Type Safety
- Always use the UserRole enum for role assignments
- Validate role-specific fields based on user type
- Use TypeScript interfaces for type checking
- Handle optional fields appropriately
